---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PlannerCTA from '../../components/PlannerCTA.astro';

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is Redwood Outdoors worth considering for an outdoor sauna?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Redwood Outdoors is worth comparing when you want an outdoor kit in a barrel, cabin, or cube-style format and prefer heat-treated wood. Compare the exact model's dimensions, heater package, delivery terms, warranty, installation needs, and total project cost before deciding."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How long is the Redwood Outdoors sauna warranty?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Redwood Outdoors currently publishes a one-year limited warranty for wooden saunas. The warranty has exclusions and does not generally cover labor, installation, electrician, contractor, rigging, permit, or other third-party costs. Read the current warranty for the exact product before purchase."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How are Redwood Outdoors saunas delivered?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Redwood Outdoors states that its default delivery method is curbside freight delivery. Delivery appointments are generally required, shipping charges are shown before purchase, and buyers should inspect the shipment and document damage on the delivery paperwork."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---
<Base
  title="Redwood Outdoors Sauna Review (2026): Buyer Checklist"
  description="A current Redwood Outdoors sauna review covering the outdoor lineup, heat-treated hemlock, warranty, freight delivery, heater choices, and total project cost."
  canonical="/brands/redwood-outdoors-sauna-review"
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700 mb-3">Outdoor sauna brand review</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Redwood Outdoors Sauna Review</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-600 mb-3">A verification-first look at the current lineup, delivery process, warranty, and costs that sit outside the product price.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">Reviewed August 2026 &middot; Backyard Sauna Pro</p>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-xl p-5 mb-8 text-sm text-stone-700">
      <strong>Commercial disclosure:</strong> Redwood Outdoors links on this page go directly to the retailer. We do not currently have a verified commission-bearing relationship with Redwood Outdoors. This is a desk-researched review, not a claim of hands-on testing.
    </div>

    <section class="bg-stone-900 text-white rounded-xl p-6 mb-8">
      <p class="text-amber-300 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Quick verdict</p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">A broad outdoor lineup, with project details to verify</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-200 mb-4">Redwood Outdoors is worth a shortlist if you want a heat-treated wood kit in a barrel, cabin, or cube-style format. Its current collection covers small two-person models through larger group saunas. That variety is useful.</p>
      <p class="text-stone-200 mb-5">The harder question is not whether the catalog looks good. It is whether the exact model, heater package, curbside delivery, site work, electrical plan, and one-year limited sauna warranty fit your project.</p>
      <a href="https://www.redwoodoutdoors.com/collections/saunas" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="inline-block bg-amber-400 hover:bg-amber-500 text-stone-900 font-semibold px-5 py-3 rounded-lg" data-cta-position="above_fold">Check the current Redwood lineup</a>
    </section>

    <PlannerCTA
      source="redwood_brand_review_after_verdict"
      heading="Compare the Redwood model with the rest of the project"
      description="Capture the site, delivery access, base, heater package, electrical plan, installation help, budget, and timeline before requesting a complete quote."
    />

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">What Redwood Outdoors sells now</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">The current sauna collection includes outdoor barrel, cabin, and cube-style products, plus indoor models. Redwood lists capacities from two people to larger six- and eight-person configurations. Product names, stock, heater packages, and promotions can change, so use the collection as the source of truth at the time you buy.</p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
      <table class="text-sm w-full">
        <thead>
          <tr class="text-left text-stone-500 border-b border-stone-200">
            <th class="pb-2 pr-5">Current example</th>
            <th class="pb-2 pr-5">Format</th>
            <th class="pb-2">Useful for</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-stone-700">
          <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-3 pr-5 font-medium">Duo</td><td class="py-3 pr-5">2-person outdoor cabin</td><td class="py-3">A compact site where exterior footprint matters</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-stone-100"><td class="py-3 pr-5 font-medium">Cabin</td><td class="py-3 pr-5">4-person outdoor cabin</td><td class="py-3">Buyers who want a rectangular room rather than a barrel</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-3 pr-5 font-medium">Extra-Wide</td><td class="py-3 pr-5">6-person outdoor barrel</td><td class="py-3">A larger barrel layout, with or without a porch option</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-8">Sources: Redwood Outdoors' current <a href="https://www.redwoodoutdoors.com/collections/saunas" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">sauna collection</a> and the official <a href="https://www.redwoodoutdoors.com/pages/assembly" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">assembly-manual library</a>.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Heat-treated hemlock: what the claim means</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Current Redwood product pages describe their sauna wood as heat-treated hemlock. Redwood says the treatment removes moisture and improves stability, durability, and resistance to moisture, decay, and insects. Those are manufacturer claims, not findings from our own weathering test.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">The practical takeaway is simple: ask what finish and maintenance the exact model needs in your climate. A wood treatment does not make roofing, drainage, ventilation, foundation work, or routine drying irrelevant.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-8">Source: Redwood Outdoors' current <a href="https://www.redwoodoutdoors.com/pages/thermowood" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Thermowood explanation</a>.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">The price tag is not the project cost</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">A configured sauna may require a heater package, controller, stones, safety railing, roofing, foundation work, electrical labor, permits, freight access, and on-site assembly. Some choices appear as product-page add-ons. Others will come from local contractors.</p>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-6">Redwood's product pages currently offer several heater families and wattages. Do not treat those menus as an electrical design. Match the final heater to the finished room and have a qualified electrician confirm the circuit, wiring, disconnects, clearances, and local requirements.</p>

    <div class="bg-emerald-50 border border-emerald-200 rounded-xl p-6 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Estimate the complete project first</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">Use the project calculator for the sauna kit, freight, foundation, electrical work, installation, accessories, tax, and maintenance. It is a planning aid, not a contractor quote or engineering approval.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/tools/sauna-cost-calculator/" class="inline-block bg-emerald-800 hover:bg-emerald-900 text-white font-semibold px-5 py-3 rounded-lg" data-cta-position="project_cost">Estimate project cost</a>
        <a href="/sauna-planner/?ref=redwood_review&campaign=planner_first_10&placement=redwood_project_brief" class="inline-block border border-emerald-700 text-emerald-900 hover:bg-emerald-100 font-semibold px-5 py-3 rounded-lg" data-track-event="planner_cta_clicked" data-cta-position="redwood_project_brief">Build a project brief</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Delivery and warranty checks</h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-8">
      <div class="border border-stone-200 rounded-lg p-5 bg-white">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Freight delivery</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">Redwood states that curbside freight is the default. An appointment is generally required. Check truck access, crate handling, storage, and the route from the curb to the build site before ordering.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-stone-200 rounded-lg p-5 bg-white">
        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">One-year limited sauna warranty</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-700">The current wooden-sauna warranty lasts one year from delivery. It has exclusions and generally does not cover labor, electrical work, contractors, permits, rigging, or other third-party costs.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-8">Read the current official <a href="https://www.redwoodoutdoors.com/pages/shipping-returns" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">shipping and returns policy</a> and <a href="https://www.redwoodoutdoors.com/pages/warranty-saunas" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">sauna warranty</a> before purchase.</p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">Who should shortlist Redwood Outdoors?</h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5 mb-8">
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-emerald-800 mb-2">Shortlist it if you:</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700">
          <li>want an outdoor kit in a barrel, cabin, or cube-style format;</li>
          <li>prefer heat-treated hemlock over untreated wood;</li>
          <li>can plan for curbside freight and on-site assembly;</li>
          <li>will compare complete installed cost, not the base price alone.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold text-rose-800 mb-2">Keep comparing if you:</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700">
          <li>need a longer sauna warranty;</li>
          <li>want white-glove delivery or turnkey installation included;</li>
          <li>have not confirmed the heater and electrical plan;</li>
          <li>need a project that fits a strict all-in budget.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mt-10 mb-4">FAQ</h2>
    <div class="space-y-5">
      <div><h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">Is Redwood Outdoors worth considering?</h3><p class="text-stone-700">Yes, when its current formats, heat-treated wood, and heater choices fit your site. Compare the exact model on dimensions, delivery, warranty, electrical requirements, and installed cost.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">How long is the sauna warranty?</h3><p class="text-stone-700">Redwood currently publishes a one-year limited warranty for wooden saunas. Read the exclusions and remedy terms before ordering.</p></div>
      <div><h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-1">Does Redwood install the sauna?</h3><p class="text-stone-700">Do not assume installation is included. The products are sold as on-site assembly kits, while freight, site preparation, electrical work, and assembly arrangements depend on the order and your location.</p></div>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-stone-50 border border-stone-200 rounded-xl p-6 mt-10">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Continue comparing</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/guides/redwood-outdoors-vs-almost-heaven/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Redwood Outdoors vs Almost Heaven</a></li>
        <li><a href="/brands/almost-heaven-sauna-review/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Almost Heaven sauna review</a></li>
        <li><a href="/brands/dundalk-leisurecraft-review/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Dundalk LeisureCraft review</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/outdoor-sauna-buying-checklist/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">Outdoor sauna buying checklist</a></li>
        <li><a href="/how-we-review/" class="text-amber-700 hover:underline">How we research sauna products</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
